lls show Kreiss-Tomkins ahead by three to eight points, prediction markets price his win odds near 77-87 percent, and raters lean Democratic despite calling it a toss-up. The Republican consolidation push under Alaska's ranked-choice system is the main counterweight, so uncertainty stays wide.", "watch": "If the Wilson-Bronson ranking pact fully consolidates Republican support behind Taylor, or new polling shows the field shifting, the race could move back toward the GOP.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Mike Dunleavy (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Alaska's governorship is open as Republican Mike Dunleavy terms out, and the race has become an unexpected Democratic opportunity. Jonathan Kreiss-Tomkins faces three Republicans — Treg Taylor, Bernadette Wilson and Dave Bronson — under the state's ranked-choice system. Recent polls show Kreiss-Tomkins ahead by roughly three to eight points, though large swaths of voters remain undecided. Most race raters call it a toss-up, while prediction markets lean clearly toward the Democrat, pricing his win odds near 77 to 87 percent.\n\nKreiss-Tomkins has raised more than $2 million and drawn $650,000 in outside support, and the national climate appears to be weighing on Republicans. The main counterweight is consolidation: Wilson and Bronson have urged their supporters to rank Republicans ahead of him, and a unified Republican vote could overtake his first-round lead. Uncertainty is high, but the current evidence tilts Democratic.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6825, "margin": 2.46}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7335, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7395, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7331, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7068, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7071, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7313, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7365, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-